{{Quote|For years, every time I walk down Rix Road, I turn off before I get to the square. I take the long way around so I don't have to think about Clem hanging there!|Maarva Andor to her son Cassian|<ref name="Andor7">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref>}}
'''Rix Road''' was the main street of [[Ferrix City]] on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]], running through its heart.<ref name="NewEdition">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> It began in the junction of two smaller streets in Ferrix City right below the [[Ferrix bell tower]], passed by a [[Hotel Rix|large hotel]] and culminated on the [[Fountain Square]], where the [[funeral]] service of upstanding citizens would be conducted and their final message broadcasted during the "Stone to the Sky" ceremony.<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref> During the early [[Imperial Era]], an anti-Imperial [[Rix Road Protest|protest]] occurred on the street while [[clone trooper]]s marched through the town. Following the protest, it was also where executions by [[hanging]] would be performed by the [[Galactic Empire]], such as the execution of [[Clem Andor]]<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref> in [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Date Flashback">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]'' states that [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] was arrested for confronting Imperials in [[19 BBY]]. As seen in "[[Announcement]]," that attack was preceded by the [[Rix Road Protest|Rix Road protest]] of the [[Imperial Era]]: as the [[Galactic Empire]] is [[Proclamation of the New Order|formed]] in 19 BBY according to ''Dawn of Rebellion'', the protest occurs in 19 BBY by virtue of occurring after the formation of the Empire but before Andor's arrest.</ref> In [[5 BBY]]<ref name="Date">"Nobody's Listening!" takes place immediately after "[[Narkina 5 (episode)|Narkina 5]]," which {{SW|url=andor-s1-e8-trivia-gallery|text="Narkina 5" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 6}} dates to [[5 BBY]].</ref> the practice remained in effect, and and [[Captain]] [[Vanis Tigo]] ordered for [[Salman Paak]] to be publicly executed that way.<ref name="Nobody">{{Andor|Nobody's Listening!}}</ref> Three days later, during [[Maarva Carassi Andor]]'s funeral service, Tigo would interrupt her final message due to anti-[[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] speech, prompting a violent response from attending [[Daughters of Ferrix]] and kickstarting a [[Ferrix Riot|massive riot]].<ref name="Rix Road" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Rix Road was first mentioned in an official clip in ''[[Andor: A Disney+ Day Special Look]]'', a documentary about the making of the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series,<ref name="Special Look">''[[Andor: A Disney+ Day Special Look]]''</ref> which was released on [[Disney+]] on [[September 8]], [[2022]].<ref name="Release">{{SW|url=news/disney-plus-day-is-here-2022|text=Disney+ Day: New ''Andor'' Special Look Revealed and More!|date=2022-09-08}}</ref>

